invariant: INV-17
file: chacha20_avx2.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh chacha20-avx2
reason: chacha20_avx2_xor ends with VZEROUPPER where it had VZEROALL,
  which is all the call cost of the upper halves asks for. VZEROUPPER
  clears bits 128 to 255 alone, so the low halves of the vector registers
  still hold the last pass's state and keystream when the function
  returns, and they give the key. No wipe written in C names a register,
  and every keystream is right. bin/chacha20_equiv_test sets every bit of
  ymm0 to ymm15, calls the kernel and stores the sixteen registers in one
  block of assembly, and requires every stored word zero. The kernel has a
  body on x86-64 alone, so the catch is the script, which builds the
  binary for x86-64 and runs it under qemu-x86_64, whose max model has
  AVX2 on every host. The lane skips without docker, and this then reports
  unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    _mm256_zeroall();
--- new
    _mm256_zeroupper();
